    "faq_section_bjxzKR": {
      "type": "faq-section",
      "blocks": {
        "collapsible_row_4VGV9b": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "When will I see results?",
            "row_content": "<p>Everyone's journey is different. Most people begin to see a change within four to eight weeks, when the medication is combined with our recommended nutrition and exercise guidelines. <\/p><p>The pace depends on you, your medication and how you approach the lifestyle changes. Consistency matters more than speed, and we're here to keep you motivated every step of the way.<\/p>"
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_bzzp7L": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What is the difference between Mounjaro and Wegovy? ",
            "row_content": "<p>Both are clinically proven weight-loss medications that are injected weekly. But they work differently. <\/p><p>Wegovy contains semaglutide, which mimics the single hormone glucagon-like peptide (GLP-1) to reduce cravings and help you feel fuller for longer. Mounjaro contains tirzepatide, which targets the two hormones GLP-1 and glucose-dependent insulinotropic polypeptide (GIP) simultaneously to slow digestion, reduce appetite and help you feel fuller for longer. Individual results vary with both medications. <\/p><p>The right choice depends on your health history, your body and your goals. And that’s what we’re here for. Your clinician will assess this during your consultation to find the most effective medication for you. <\/p>"
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_C9p89w": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Can I use weight-loss medication long term? ",
            "row_content": "<p>Yes — both Wegovy and Mounjaro may be used long-term as part of a personalised weight-loss pathway. The lifestyle habits you build during treatment are just as important as the medication itself, and your settlehealth pathway is designed to support both. Your clinician will review your treatment regularly to make sure it continues to work effectively for you.<\/p>"
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_VqL7ez": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What happens when I stop treatment? ",
            "row_content": "<p>It's important to be honest about this. Research shows that stopping GLP-1 medication can lead to weight regain in many people — often because the hormonal drivers of appetite and metabolism return to their previous state. <\/p><p>This is why the lifestyle changes you make during treatment are so important. At settlehealth, your treatment pathway isn't just about the medication — it's about building sustainable habits that support you long after treatment ends. Maintaining a healthy diet with regular exercise will help you keep the weight off long-term. Any decision to stop should always be made with your clinician, not alone.<\/p>"
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_ALMQgt": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Why is settlehealth different from just taking medication alone? ",
            "row_content": "<p>Medication is a powerful tool, but it’s most effective when combined with a whole-person approach. <\/p><p>Your personalised treatment pathway is individually designed by a specialised clinician who understands your health history, your goals and your individual response to treatment. This includes ongoing support, regular reviews, nutritional guidance and a personal dashboard to track your progress. The medication creates the conditions for change. The pathway is what makes that change last.<\/p>"
          }
        }
      },
